From: Long Way Home <noreply@long-way-home.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] triggers may be boxes

A trigger needs a volume, not geometry, but every trigger in the released game takes its volume
from a brush model. On a whole ship that is 500 brush models spent on boxes. A trigger written with
"mins" and "maxs" and no brush model is now a plain box at its origin; one with a brush model
behaves exactly as before.
---
diff --git a/efgame/src/game/g_trigger.cpp b/efgame/src/game/g_trigger.cpp
--- a/efgame/src/game/g_trigger.cpp
+++ b/efgame/src/game/g_trigger.cpp
@@ -13,7 +13,12 @@
 	if (!VectorCompare (self->s.angles, vec3_origin))
 		G_SetMovedir (self->s.angles, self->movedir);
 
-	gi.SetBrushModel( self, self->model );
+	// A trigger needs a volume, not geometry. One written with "mins"/"maxs" and no brush model is a
+	// plain box at its origin, and costs the map no brush model at all.
+	if ( self->model && self->model[0] == '*' )
+	{
+		gi.SetBrushModel( self, self->model );
+	}
 	self->contents = CONTENTS_TRIGGER;		// replaces the -1 from gi.SetBrushModel
 	self->svFlags = SVF_NOCLIENT;
 
